  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Monday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: A mix of wintry precipitation will \npersist in portions of our eastern counties this morning, as a \ndeep trough is working it\u2019s way out of our area. This has allowed \nus to wake up this morning to snow capped mountains, and for some,\nearly season snow capped driveways. As this system continues to \nwork east, gradual clearing will appear throughout the watch area,\nbringing us back to our seasonably appropriate, dry weather. \nHighs will start off today around the mid 40s to 50s, before \ngradually increasing the remainder of the week, with lows well below \nnormal. Lows will range from the upper teens over northern NV to \nlower 30s further south. The lows for tonight are especially \nsignificant, as most of the area will see lows 10-15 degrees below \nnormal, marking the first time this season we have seen these \nwidespread subfreezing temps. \n\nAs we progress Thursday into Friday, a ridge will attempt to set up\nover our area, with a weak subtropical low setting up along the \nNV, CA, and AZ borders. This will set us up for seasonable weather\nwithin the watch area, leaving us with mostly sunny skies and \nhighs in the 50s and 60s, before increasing to the mid 60s to 70s \nas we enter the very pleasant weekend. \n\nLooking at our next set-up, those of us who greatly enjoy winter\nweather will be very pleased as a polar jet has the potential of\nworking it\u2019s way back into our area, replacing the weak blocking\nlow regime. This will contain a deep low bringing a strong cold\nfront through our area early next week, dropping highs back down\nto the 40s and 50s, and our lows into the 20s and 30s. This front\nwill have the potential to bring precipitation next Monday and\nTuesday, but confidence in timing and amounts are low as we are\nstill a full week away.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in the general\nclearing of sky cover and wintry precipitation today. High \nconfidence in dry and warming conditions starting tomorrow. \nModerate confidence in temperatures decreasing along the front \nnext week. Low confidence in precipitation types, placement, and \ntiming next week.",
